            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0350" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/1747: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-23T18:00:00-05:00">November 23, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>94. Your 78, November 23, 2 p.m. <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi>
                    report is complete misinterpretation of certain provisions of debt bill,
                    translation of which is given in my telegram 96, November 23, 10 p.m.<anchor
                        n="50" xml:id="d221-f1"/> Bill does not affect payment of duties.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
